<% content_for :title, 'Arborist CRM' %>
<% content_for :description, 'Big Tree Services is a CRM for arborist and tree care businesses: estimates, quoting, tree inventories, crew scheduling, invoicing and receipts in one place.' %>

<section class="hero">
  <h1>The CRM built for tree care work</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Big Tree Services is a web application that arborist and tree care companies use to run
    the job from first site visit to final invoice &mdash; estimates, tree inventories,
    quotes, crew scheduling, invoicing and expense tracking in one place.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="btn" href="/login">Sign in to your account</a>
    <a href="mailto:info@bigtreeservices.ca">Contact us</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>What the application does</h2>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Estimates &amp; site visits</h3>
      <p>Book estimate appointments, capture site details and assign a certified arborist to attend.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Tree inventories</h3>
      <p>Record each tree on a property with species, condition, planned work actions and photographs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Quoting</h3>
      <p>Build a costed quote from the tree list and send it to the customer as a branded PDF.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Scheduling &amp; dispatch</h3>
      <p>Schedule approved work, assign crews and equipment, and track job progress in the field.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Invoicing &amp; payments</h3>
      <p>Raise final invoices from completed work, issue receipts and follow up on outstanding balances.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Hours &amp; expenses</h3>
      <p>Log crew hours, capture receipts and equipment requests, and export reporting for payroll.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Who uses it</h2>
  <p>
    Big Tree Services is a business tool, not a consumer product. Its users are the staff of a
    tree care company: office administrators who manage the schedule and the books, and
    certified arborists and crew members who carry out the work. Each company is a separate
    tenant, and staff only ever see the data belonging to the company that invited them.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Email integration</h2>
  <p>
    Quotes, invoices, receipts and appointment notices need to reach the customer from the
    tree care company's own address &mdash; not from a generic no-reply mailbox. So a company
    administrator can connect the company's Google Workspace or Microsoft 365 mailbox to
    their account, and the application then sends those documents on the company's behalf.
  </p>
  <p>
    The connection is made using OAuth, through our email infrastructure provider
    <a href="https://www.nylas.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Nylas</a>. No mailbox
    password is ever entered into or stored by the application, and an administrator can
    disconnect the mailbox at any time from the company settings page, which revokes our
    access immediately.
  </p>

  <h3>What we ask for, and what we do with it</h3>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="scopes">
      <tr>
        <th>Access requested</th>
        <th>Why</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Send mail on your behalf</td>
        <td>
          To deliver quotes, invoices, receipts, appointment confirmations and job updates
          to your customers from your own business address, with the relevant PDF attached.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Basic account details (email address)</td>
        <td>
          To show the connected sending address in your settings and to confirm the
          connection is still valid before each send.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>We do not read your mailbox.</strong> The application does not request or use
      access to read, search, download or delete your existing mail, and it does not access
      your contacts, calendars or files. Of each message it sends, it keeps only a record
      that the send happened: the recipient address, the time, the type of document sent and
      the provider's message identifier.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Our use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google
    API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements. The
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> sets out in full what we collect, how long we keep
    it and who we share it with.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    For access, support, security reports or privacy requests, email
    <a href="mailto:info@bigtreeservices.ca">info@bigtreeservices.ca</a>. We aim to respond
    to all enquiries within five business days.
  </p>
</section>
